From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:22:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] media: i2c: hi847: Add OF support, power management, 24
 MHz MCLK, module EEPROM

Make the driver usable on DT systems such as the Unihertz Titan 2:

- OF match "hynix,hi847";
- optional reset and powerdown GPIOs, avdd/dovdd/dvdd supplies and a
  runtime PM power sequence (MCLK, PDN low 1 ms, RST low 1 ms, DOVDD
  3 ms, AVDD 1 ms, DVDD 1 ms, RST high 2 ms, PDN high 2 ms; power off in
  reverse without delays); on ACPI the sensor is only touched at probe
  when it is in D0, as in hi556;
- orientation and rotation controls from the firmware node;
- a 24 MHz MCLK configuration with its own mode tables (3264x2448@30
  and 1920x1080@60), link frequencies 500 and 400 MHz, 24-bit exposure
  and frame length writes, group hold (0x0208) around exposure, gain and
  vblank updates, and the limits of that module. Flip controls stay with
  the 19.2 MHz tables only, as they rewrite output offsets that the 1080p
  crop uses;
- the calibration EEPROM of the camera module (same bus, 0x50 by default,
  answers only while the module is powered) is read once at probe and
  offered as a read-only nvmem device for user-space calibration
  (mtk-module-eeprom.h, shared with the IMX766 driver).

The 19.2 MHz behaviour is unchanged apart from the power handling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
