+/*
+ * TODO: link frequencies of the 24 MHz tables are derived, not
+ * specified. Registers 0x0744..0x0748 (125 for 3264x2448, 100 for 1080p,
+ * pre-divider 2) give 24 * 125 / 3 = 1000 and 24 * 100 / 3 = 800 Mbit/s per
+ * lane, i.e. 500 and 400 MHz; the 19.2 MHz table gives 19.2 * 125 / 3 = 800,
+ * matching HI847_LINK_FREQ_400MHZ. The MIPI timing registers 0x1022..0x102c
+ * scale the same way. The factory csi_pixel_rate (400 Mpixel/s for both modes)
+ * only matches the 3264x2448 mode.
+ */
